    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Fellow Workers is an album by American folksinger Utah Phillips and American singer-songwriter Ani DiFranco.\n[2] Ani DiFranco ( ; born Angela Maria DiFranco; September 23, 1970) is an American singer, multi-instrumentalist, poet, songwriter and businesswoman.\n[3] Like I Said: Songs 1990–91 is a 1994 album by Ani DiFranco, offering reinterpretations of songs from her first two albums, the eponymous \"Ani DiFranco\" (1990) and \"Not So Soft\" (1991).\n[4] DiFranco re-recorded five songs that had been previously released: \"Both Hands\", \"Overlap\", \"Napoleon\", \"Shameless\" and \"Your Next Bold Move\"."
